# layout.x86_64-windows.golden: expected SizeOf, AlignOf and offsets for tests/conformance/diff/layout.mk (TestDiffLayout).
# Format: <Name> <size> <align> [<offset>...], one line per Layout<Name> function, in the file's order.
# Written by hand from Mk's own layout rules (those for slices, str, enums, optionals, results,
# records, Cell) and, for the C-shaped parts (scalars, struct padding, packed), the Microsoft x64 calling convention and data layout (Win64): every scalar aligned to its size, pointers 8.
# The four goldens are equal: these types have the same sizes and alignments on all four targets. No clang cross-check was run.
I8 1 1
I16 2 2
I32 4 4
I64 8 8
U8 1 1
U16 2 2
U32 4 4
U64 8 8
Int 8 8
Uint 8 8
F32 4 4
F64 8 8
Bool 1 1
Char 4 4
RefI32 8 8
SliceU8 16 8 0 8
SliceI64 16 8 0 8
Str 16 8 0 8
ArrayU16 6 2 0 2 4
ArrayPair 32 8 0 16
Fn 8 8
Pair 16 8 0 8
Mixed 16 4 0 2 4 8 12
Nested 24 8 0 16
Tail 8 4 0 4
PackedMixed 9 1 0 1 3 4 8
Packed2Mixed 12 2 0 2 4 6 10
Record 16 8 0 8
Color 1 1
Level 2 2
Code 4 4
Shape 16 8 0 8
Tok 4 2 0 2
OptRef 8 8
OptI32 8 4 0 4
OptU8 2 1 0 1
OptPair 24 8 0 8
BadI64 16 8 0 8
BadU8 8 4 0 4
BigU8 16 8 0 4 8
CellI32 4 4
PageTable 4096 4096
Align16 16 16
Align64Pair 64 64 0 8
Align1 4 4
HoldsAligned 32 16 0 16
VecF32x4 16 4
VecU8x32 32 1
MaskF64x2 16 8
HoldsVec 20 4 0 4
